1
00:00:01,160 --> 00:00:12,480
Misato: Are you ready Shinji?

2
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:12,480
Shinji: Um yeah.

3
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:12,480
Misato: Final safety locks, release!

4
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:12,480
Misato: Evangelion Unit-01, move out!

5
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:12,480
Ritsuko: Shinji, just oncentrate on walking for now.

6
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:12,480
Ritsuko: Uh. Walk.

7
00:02:00,320 --> 00:02:00,940
Ritsuko: He's walking!

8
00:02:03,960 --> 00:02:04,680
Shinji: Walking.

9
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:13,780
Misato: Shiji! Are you okay?

10
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:15,980
Misato: Hurry! Hurry!

11
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:17,440
Misato: You've got to get out!

12
00:02:17,700 --> 00:02:17,720
Shinji: Oh!

13
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:23,000
Shinji: Oh! Ohhh.

14
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:31,980
Misato: Shinji, calm down! That's not your real arm!

15
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:38,000
Ritsuko: Where is defense system?

16
00:02:38,280 --> 00:02:39,400
Makoto: The signal's not working!

17
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,700
Makoto: His field's not up! It's not unfolding!

18
00:02:41,980 --> 00:02:42,800
Ritsuko: It's not up?

19
00:02:47,460 --> 00:02:48,460
Ibuki: Left arm damaged!

20
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:49,800
Makoto: The circuits are snapped!

21
00:02:52,900 --> 00:02:53,740
Misato: Shinji, move!

22
00:02:53,740 --> 00:02:53,740
Shinji: Whoa! Ahh!

23
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:01,680
Ibuki: There's a crack on the front of the brain cases.

24
00:03:02,260 --> 00:03:03,560
Ritsuko: That armor won't take much more.

25
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:15,000
Makoto: The head is damaged, extended damage, unknown!

26
00:03:15,220 --> 00:03:16,640
Ibuki: The controllers are breaking up.

27
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:18,420
Aoba: We're not getting any ratings on the pilot.

28
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:20,680
Misato: No, Shiji!

29
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:20,680
Shinji: Ah!

30
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:20,680
Ibuki: Cicadas Droning

31
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:54,260
Ritsuko: Unfamiliar ceiling.

32
00:04:08,660 --> 00:04:10,940
US Representative Green: So, the angels have returned.

33
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:12,420
US Representative Green: It's rather sudden.

34
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:15,700
Male Voice: It's the same as it was 15 years ago.

35
00:04:16,799 --> 00:04:17,959
Male Voice: That's the way of disasters.

36
00:04:18,079 --> 00:04:19,459
Male Voice: They come without warning.

37
00:04:20,079 --> 00:04:25,520
UK Representative Red: On the positive side, our previous investments would appear to be not such a waste after all.

38
00:04:25,880 --> 00:04:27,620
Russia Representative Purple: You can't be sure about that yet.

39
00:04:28,420 --> 00:04:30,800
Russia Representative Purple: If it doesn't pay off, it's still a waste.

40
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:31,420
French Representative Yellow: Correct.

41
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:35,220
French Representative Yellow: Now that news of the Angels has become common knowledge,

42
00:04:36,260 --> 00:04:42,660
French Representative Yellow: Nerve must take steps to control the manner in which this information is received by the general public.

43
00:04:43,940 --> 00:04:46,880
Gendo: You may rest assured that it's already been taken care of.

44
00:04:47,460 --> 00:04:47,940
Gendo: Don't worry.

45
00:04:47,940 --> 00:04:47,940
Gendo: Government officials have announced that

46
00:04:47,940 --> 00:04:47,940
Gendo: This incident

47
00:04:55,740 --> 00:04:57,760
Misato: Public scenario B-22.

48
00:04:58,260 --> 00:04:59,180
Misato: Just like we thought.

49
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:01,420
Misato: So we're covering up the truth again?

50
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:04,040
Ritsuko: Well, at least the PR people are happy.

51
00:05:04,420 --> 00:05:05,900
Ritsuko: They finally got something to do.

52
00:05:06,140 --> 00:05:08,260
Misato: We're being pretty casual about it.

53
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:10,020
Misato: I don't think so.

54
00:05:10,580 --> 00:05:12,280
Misato: Actually, I think we're all pretty scared.

55
00:05:12,760 --> 00:05:13,860
Shinji: Of course we are.

56
00:05:14,660 --> 00:05:16,780
Russia Representative Purple: Well, we must acknowledge that.

57
00:05:17,180 --> 00:05:22,420
US Representative Green: But still, I wonder, Mr. Ikari, were Nerve and Eva used efficiently?

58
00:05:22,980 --> 00:05:29,700
French Representative Yellow: Repair costs for Unit-01 added to the development costs for Unit-00 are simply staggering.

59
00:05:30,260 --> 00:05:34,300
UK Representative Red: We also understand that you gave that toy to your own son.

60
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:37,460
Russia Representative Purple: Time, money, and manpower.

61
00:05:38,460 --> 00:05:41,060
Russia Representative Purple: How much more will be wasted by you and your family?

62
00:05:41,520 --> 00:05:43,620
UK Representative Red: And that is not your only responsibility.

63
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:47,700
UK Representative Red: The Human Enhancement Project. That should be your top priority.

64
00:05:48,420 --> 00:05:56,180
French Representative Yellow: Correct. Under these desperate circumstances, that project may be the only real hope for the future of mankind. Do you understand?

65
00:05:57,020 --> 00:06:01,860
Keel Lorenz: In any event, the Angels are no excuse for the delay in the schedule of that project.

66
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:05,240
Keel Lorenz: We may consider adjusting the budget.

67
00:06:05,420 --> 00:06:07,640
US Representative Green: The rest of the meeting does not concern you.

68
00:06:07,660 --> 00:06:10,340
French Representative Yellow: Your presence here was... appreciated.

69
00:06:12,340 --> 00:06:15,920
Keel Lorenz: Ikari, you do know that there can be no turning back.

70
00:06:18,580 --> 00:06:19,680
Gendo: I know.

71
00:06:21,760 --> 00:06:23,840
Gendo: Mankind has no time left.

72
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:53,600
US Representative Green: Man, air conditioning's the greatest thing.

73
00:06:54,060 --> 00:06:55,540
US Representative Green: Man's Triumph over nature!

74
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:58,040
Ritsuko: Shinji's finally woken up!

75
00:06:59,460 --> 00:07:01,040
Misato: And... how is he?

76
00:07:01,780 --> 00:07:04,720
Ritsuko: Well, his memory seems a bit muddled, but...

77
00:07:04,720 --> 00:07:06,580
Misato: You don't think it could be contamination, do you?

78
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:08,720
Ritsuko: I don't think we should worry.

79
00:07:09,820 --> 00:07:09,980
Misato: Really?

80
00:07:12,260 --> 00:07:14,740
Misato: You're right. He did have a pretty hectic day.

81
00:07:15,080 --> 00:07:18,640
Ritsuko: Poor little kid. His cerebellum must have taken a lot of stress.

82
00:07:19,820 --> 00:07:21,600
Misato: Cerebellum? Don't you mean his heart?

83
00:07:49,420 --> 00:07:53,480
Misato: If Eva and this city both operated their full potential, we might make it through this.

84
00:07:54,280 --> 00:07:55,800
Ritsuko: You're such an optimist.

85
00:07:56,300 --> 00:08:00,200
Misato: Hey, sometimes you need a little wishful thinking just to keep on living.

86
00:08:00,700 --> 00:08:05,700
Ritsuko: I see your point. It's nice to hear a positive attitude. I'll see you later.

87
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:07,780
Misato: Okay, see ya.

88
00:08:09,380 --> 00:08:13,500
Female Voice: Dr. Uga'i, Internal Department 1. Dr. Uga'i, Internal Department 1.

89
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:17,240
Female Voice: Please call Dr. Azuma of the First Surgical Department immediately.

90
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:22,420
Female Voice: The medical conference regarding the B experiment will be held as scheduled.

91
00:08:22,860 --> 00:08:25,940
Female Voice: All supervisors, please proceed to conference room two.

92
00:08:47,860 --> 00:08:50,520
Ritsuko: They don't want to live together? Are you sure?

93
00:08:51,160 --> 00:08:54,080
Fuyutski: I think that living apart is natural to them.

94
00:08:54,820 --> 00:08:56,960
Ritsuko: And being together is unnatural?

95
00:09:00,920 --> 00:09:01,780
Misato: You'll be living alone?

96
00:09:02,340 --> 00:09:06,240
Male Voice: That's right. His room will be on the sixth block beyond this one. Is that alright?

97
00:09:07,140 --> 00:09:07,580
Shinji: Yes, sir.

98
00:09:09,300 --> 00:09:11,600
Misato: Shinji, are you sure about that?

99
00:09:12,420 --> 00:09:16,260
Shinji: Living alone is fine with me. I'm alone anyway.

100
00:09:18,020 --> 00:09:18,780
Ritsuko: What did you say?

101
00:09:18,940 --> 00:09:22,940
Misato: You heard me! I said I'll be taking Shinji home to live in my place, okay?

102
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:24,980
Misato: It's already been approved.

103
00:09:26,020 --> 00:09:29,080
Misato: And don't worry, I'm not gonna be making any passes at him.

104
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:31,780
Ritsuko: Of course you're not! How could you even think of such a thing?

105
00:09:32,020 --> 00:09:33,080
Ritsuko: You've got no shame at all!

106
00:09:33,100 --> 00:09:35,140
Misato: Some people don't have any sense of humor.

107
00:09:40,579 --> 00:09:43,240
Misato: Well, I guess we have to have a party tonight, huh?

108
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:44,520
Shinji: Why is that?

109
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:47,800
Shinji: It's a welcoming party in honor of my new roommate, of course

110
00:10:04,340 --> 00:10:07,020
Female Voice: Yes, I'd never have dreamt that this city would become a battlefield

111
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:10,740
Woman 2: Yeah, my husband's saying that at least the kids and I should move.

112
00:10:11,240 --> 00:10:11,700
Female Voice: Don't I know it

113
00:10:11,820 --> 00:10:14,740
Female Voice: This city may be a fortress, but that's no guarantee of safety.

114
00:10:15,260 --> 00:10:17,340
Woman 2: Just thinking about last night gives me the chills.

115
00:10:21,520 --> 00:10:24,460
Misato: I hope you don't mind if we make a little stop on the way.

116
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:25,900
Shinji: A stop where?

117
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:28,500
US Representative Green: Oh, it's a really cool place.

118
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:34,360
Shinji: It's so desolate.

119
00:10:36,460 --> 00:10:37,980
Shinji: The city seems so lonely.

120
00:10:40,280 --> 00:10:41,020
Misato: Here we go.

121
00:11:06,940 --> 00:11:07,580
Shinji: It's awesome.

122
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:10,120
Shinji: The buildings are growing!

123
00:11:23,180 --> 00:11:26,660
Misato: This city is a fortress designed to stand against the angels.

124
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:30,660
Misato: This is Tokyo 3.

125
00:11:31,750 --> 00:11:35,340
Misato: This is our city, and it's the city that you saved.

126
00:11:35,340 --> 00:11:35,340
Misato: Your things out to have been delivered already shinji.

127
00:11:35,340 --> 00:11:35,340
Misato: Hey, come in.

128
00:12:05,700 --> 00:12:06,280
Shinji: I don't want to intrude.

129
00:12:07,220 --> 00:12:09,640
Misato: Shinji, this is *your* home now.

130
00:12:18,420 --> 00:12:19,400
Shinji: Uh. I'm...I'm home.

131
00:12:20,040 --> 00:12:21,040
Misato: Welcome home.

132
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:29,160
Misato: Um, as you can see, the place is just a little bit messy, but ahah go ahead and make yourself comfortable.

133
00:12:29,840 --> 00:12:32,100
Shinji: Um, This is a *little* messy?

134
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:37,140
Misato: Oh, sorry. Could you put the food in the fridge, please?

135
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:38,740
Shinji: Uh, yes, ma'am.

136
00:12:40,900 --> 00:12:45,780
Shinji: Ice, snacks, and 50 gallons of beer.

137
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:48,420
Shinji: What kind of life does she lead?

138
00:12:49,960 --> 00:12:50,120
Shinji: Huh.

139
00:12:55,160 --> 00:12:58,040
Shinji: Uh, excuse me. What's in the other fridge?

140
00:12:58,360 --> 00:13:00,800
Misato: Oh, don't mind that. He's probably still sleeping.

141
00:13:02,740 --> 00:13:03,060
Shinji: Sleeping?

142
00:13:05,160 --> 00:13:06,200
Misato: Let's eat!

143
00:13:07,040 --> 00:13:08,500
Shinji: Yeah, let's eat.

144
00:13:12,600 --> 00:13:16,280
Misato: Woo! Yeah! Good stuff! Uhp.

145
00:13:17,930 --> 00:13:21,220
Misato: You know, life just doesn't get any better than this.

146
00:13:22,380 --> 00:13:26,480
Misato: Hmm? Not hungry? It's good, even if it is all instant.

147
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:31,540
Shinji: I-I'm sorry. I'm just not used to food like this.

148
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:34,100
Misato: WHAT? Are you finicky?

149
00:13:34,660 --> 00:13:35,020
Misato: HM?

150
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:37,300
Shinji: Um, no. That's not what... Uh, well.

151
00:13:39,519 --> 00:13:40,620
Misato: Isn't this nice?

152
00:13:41,880 --> 00:13:43,900
Misato: Having two for dinner sure beats eating alone, ?

153
00:13:44,320 --> 00:13:44,320
Shinji: Uh huh?

154
00:13:47,060 --> 00:13:49,860
Misato: Here we go. Let's go for the next one.

155
00:13:51,420 --> 00:13:53,740
Misato: Paper, scissors, stone.

156
00:13:54,820 --> 00:13:57,940
Misato: Three, two, one, go!

157
00:13:59,420 --> 00:14:01,020
Misato: I'm sorry, Shinji.

158
00:14:02,220 --> 00:14:05,500
Misato: Okay, that was a really fair way to split up the chores, wasn't it?

159
00:14:07,100 --> 00:14:07,540
Shinji: Yeah.

160
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:11,180
Misato: This is your home, so feel free to take advantage of everything here.

161
00:14:12,060 --> 00:14:13,740
Misato: Except, of course, of me, that is.

162
00:14:14,240 --> 00:14:15,740
US Representative Green: Uh, yes, ma'am.

163
00:14:16,480 --> 00:14:17,540
Misato: Hoo. Yes, yes, yes.

164
00:14:17,970 --> 00:14:19,080
Misato: Is that all you can say?

165
00:14:19,480 --> 00:14:21,220
Misato: It's *getting* on my nerves!

166
00:14:21,540 --> 00:14:22,980
Misato: You're a bully! Act like one!

167
00:14:23,280 --> 00:14:24,000
Shinji: Yes, ma'am!

168
00:14:24,780 --> 00:14:26,860
Misato: I guess that's just the way you are.

169
00:14:27,460 --> 00:14:28,580
Misato: Why don't you go take a bath?

170
00:14:29,100 --> 00:14:31,080
Misato: Yeah! Wash away your troubles!

171
00:14:31,860 --> 00:14:33,480
Misato: Bathing cleans the mind and soul.

172
00:14:42,620 --> 00:14:43,220
Shinji: Ohoh.

173
00:14:43,220 --> 00:14:44,300
Shinji: Oh! Miss Misano! Uh pp, uh pp.

174
00:14:45,340 --> 00:14:45,760
Misato: What?

175
00:14:49,120 --> 00:14:51,940
Misato: Oh, him?

176
00:14:52,580 --> 00:14:54,240
Misato: He's one of those new warm water penguins.

177
00:15:03,220 --> 00:15:04,800
Shinji: Uhuh, That was... that was a wa-what?

178
00:15:05,140 --> 00:15:07,320
Misato: His name's Penpen. He's your other roommate.

179
00:15:10,500 --> 00:15:11,520
Misato: Why don't you cover up?

180
00:15:18,160 --> 00:15:18,680
Shinji: Ohuh?

181
00:15:18,680 --> 00:15:23,140
Misato: Huh. I guess I should be nicer, but he's probably already made up his mind about me.

182
00:15:27,200 --> 00:15:28,160
Shinji: Misato Katsaragi.

183
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:30,620
Shinji: She's not a bad person.

184
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:32,720
Misato: Bathing claims the mind and soul!

185
00:15:33,460 --> 00:15:36,100
Shinji: But bad memories always seem to find me in the bath.

186
00:15:38,380 --> 00:15:39,100
Shinji: Like my father.

187
00:15:41,120 --> 00:15:42,000
Shinji: And that girl Rei.

188
00:15:46,080 --> 00:15:47,260
Ritsuko: So how was Rei today?

189
00:15:50,280 --> 00:15:52,560
Ritsuko: You did see her at the hospital today, didn't you?

190
00:15:54,040 --> 00:15:56,020
Gendo: She can work again in 20 days.

191
00:15:57,240 --> 00:16:00,360
Gendo: By then, we'll be ready to reactivate Unit-00 from cryostasis.

192
00:16:01,580 --> 00:16:03,560
Ritsuko: It's so hard on these children.

193
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:06,160
Gendo: There's no one else who can pilot the Evas.

194
00:16:07,040 --> 00:16:10,500
Gendo: As long as they survive, that is what I'll have them do.

195
00:16:11,120 --> 00:16:13,580
Ritsuko: With no regard to what *they* may want?

196
00:16:32,020 --> 00:16:37,280
Misato: Yeahuh, after all the horrible stuff he went through, I don't think he'll pilot again.

197
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:39,880
Ritsuko: Maintaining him is part of your job.

198
00:16:40,980 --> 00:16:41,880
Misato: I'm just scared.

199
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:43,860
Misato: I don't know how to deal with him.

200
00:16:44,160 --> 00:16:45,200
Ritsuko: Grumbling already?

201
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:48,000
Ritsuko: But it was your idea to take him in, you know.

202
00:16:48,180 --> 00:16:48,940
Misato: Oh, shut up!

203
00:16:51,900 --> 00:16:54,080
Misato: Huh, I was just thinking of Shinji as a tool.

204
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:57,280
Misato: I'm as shameless as Ritsuko.

205
00:16:59,260 --> 00:17:00,880
Misato: We destroyed the angel, but...

206
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:02,960
Misato: I don't feel happy.

207
00:17:06,819 --> 00:17:08,439
Shinji: Another unfamiliar ceiling.

208
00:17:10,980 --> 00:17:15,780
Shinji: Of course, in this whole city, there's no place that's familiar.

209
00:17:16,620 --> 00:17:18,140
Misato: This is *your* home now.

210
00:17:19,520 --> 00:17:20,800
Shinji: Why am I here?

211
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:20,800
Makoto: The head is damaged. The head is damaged!

212
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:20,800
Ibuki: We're having problems maintaing activation!

213
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:20,800
Misato: Status report!

214
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:20,800
Ibuki: Syncrograph reversing.

215
00:17:47,280 --> 00:17:52,320
Ibuki: The pulses are blowing backwards!

216
00:17:52,340 --> 00:17:53,420
Ritsuko: Break the circuit now!

217
00:17:53,620 --> 00:17:54,060
Ritsuko: Do it!

218
00:17:54,220 --> 00:17:55,200
Ibuki: We can't!

219
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:56,480
Ibuki: It's not accepting the signal!

220
00:17:57,020 --> 00:17:58,200
Misato: What about Shinji?

221
00:17:58,360 --> 00:17:59,500
Makoto: His monitors aren't reacting.

222
00:17:59,900 --> 00:18:00,760
Makoto: His condition's unknown!

223
00:18:01,060 --> 00:18:02,440
Aoba: Unit 1's gone completely silent!

224
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:02,900
Ritsuko: Misato!

225
00:18:03,840 --> 00:18:05,000
Misato: We've got no choice.

226
00:18:05,300 --> 00:18:06,260
Misato: Abort the operation!

227
00:18:06,640 --> 00:18:07,880
Misato: We've got to rescue the pilot!

228
00:18:08,160 --> 00:18:09,440
Misato: Eject the entry plug!

229
00:18:09,660 --> 00:18:10,340
Ibuki: We can't!

230
00:18:10,480 --> 00:18:11,600
Ibuki: It's completely out of control!

231
00:18:11,960 --> 00:18:12,860
Misato: *What* did you say?

232
00:18:20,699 --> 00:18:22,700
Misato: The Eva's reactivating.

233
00:18:22,900 --> 00:18:24,980
Ibuki: I don't believe it! This can't be!

234
00:18:26,140 --> 00:18:27,040
Misato: My god!

235
00:18:27,500 --> 00:18:28,060
